description:
DSK Bank
is one of the leading banks in Bulgaria, with a great IT team of more than 350 IT talents, experiencing professional growth and development every day.
Now we are the biggest and fastest growing player on the bank market, and we are focused on digitalization and business growth and our new service vision towards the clients.
Your tasks in the team:
Collaborate with cross-functional teams;
Design, develop and unit test solutions of any size or complexity;
Produce clean and high-quality code;
Diagnose defects and provide effective solutions;
Take part and guide architectural decision sessions;
Support, coach and share knowledge with other team members.
You are the ideal candidate, if you have:
A bachelor’s degree and 3+ years of professional experience in Java / Kotlin;
Profile focused on backend development;
Deep knowledge and understanding of software development lifecycle best-practices, methods, and conventions like Unit and Integration Testing, Source Code Management, Continuous Integration/Continuous Delivery;
Experience in container-orchestration platforms such as Kubernetes / Openshift for large scale deployment of micro services is considered as an advantage;
Team player;
Ability to step in new technologies;
Advanced English.
What we offer to you:
Competitive multi-component remuneration and attractive bonus scheme;
An additional 102, 26 euro per month is provided in the form of food vouchers;
20+5 days paid leave;
Additional Health Insurance;
Promo price for Multisport Cards;
Perfect opportunities for professional and career development in a leading Bank in Bulgaria;
Professional trainings for specific knowledge and skills;
Unique banking service package – special loan interest for employees on housing and consumer loans;
Top technologies to use;
Discount program with external vendors;
Great working environment within a team of professionals.
If you are challenged by this opportunity, we would be glad to review your application.
Only short-listed candidates will be contacted. All applications will be treated in strict confidentiality.

SiteGround
is a
tech product and service company
powering millions of online businesses worldwide.
From
world-class web hosting
, to
SaaS platforms for site building, e-commerce, and email marketing
, we develop all our products in-house to
help businesses start, grow and succeed online more easily.
At the heart of our 20-year success is our people-driven company culture focused on performance, innovation, technical excellence, and early strategic adoption of AI.
Together, we are one of the most technically-advanced companies in our industry
, recognized by over 90 of the most prestigious business, employer, and social responsibility awards worldwide.
YOUR ROLE
:
We’re hiring a
Software Engineer
to play a pivotal role in shaping the backbone of our innovative
Software as a Service (SaaS) products
. This isn’t a typical backend role: we’re looking for someone who’s already adapted to building software in the AI era – who thinks in systems, moves comfortably across the stack, and treats AI tools as part of the craft, not a shortcut around it. Someone willing to contribute to the entire development lifecycle – from conceptualization to deployment and deliver solutions that exceed our users’ expectations in speed and reliability.
How you think, how fast you iterate, and how fearlessly you push past „good enough“
matter more to us than years logged or job titles. You’ll join a team with strong engineering proficiency that spends its time on problems that actually matter and shares a real passion for building products from the ground up, regardless of stack. We run experiments and PoC work alongside feature development on a weekly basis.
YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES:
Bring a working AI-augmented workflow into daily development – prompting, orchestrating agents, and critically reviewing AI-generated output before it ships;
Develop and maintain high-quality, scalable backend applications with appropriate backend tech like PHP, Python and Node.js, applying best practices with full ownership from design through production and performance;
Work fluently in Git within a big team, where collaboration is a must;
Partner closely with Product Managers, Front-End engineers, QAs, and DevOps to ship features end-to-end. Be responsible for systems and products that serve 3M+ websites;
Write clean, well-tested code that the next engineer can build on without fear;
Ship iteratively and often, favoring fast feedback loops and continuous improvement;
Share knowledge, challenge ideas, and continuously raise the bar for our engineering practices and the team;
Care deeply about performance, reliability, and craft – own the outcome, not just the task.
OUR EXPECTATIONS:
Demonstrate strong proficiency in using, evaluating, and experimenting with AI-based technologies to improve engineering workflows, solve complex problems, and increase development effectiveness;
Deep understanding of the HTTP stack, networking fundamentals, CI/CD pipelines, software testing, observability, and distributed systems;
Strong understanding of software architecture, APIs, databases, caching, messaging, and asynchronous processing;
Take end-to-end ownership – from the first question to a verified result in production.
Bring a strong focus on software performance and proactive extensibility;
Ability to critically evaluate technical solutions and determine whether they are the right fit for the problem, not just whether they work;
Have experience establishing engineering standards, component architectures, and development best practices;
Ability to clearly communicate technical trade-offs and complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences;
Have proven experience and scale systems that serve millions of users globally;
Ability to work effectively with ambiguity and incomplete information.
GREAT ADVANTAGE WILL BE:
If AI is an output multiplier for you;
If you are even more passionate about your work than ever before;
If you bring a team-first mindset and care more about solving the problem than proving you’re right;
If you get excited at the prospect of shipping tech products that push the web forward.
WHAT WE OFFER:
At SiteGround, we work hard and challenge ourselves to exceed expectations. To support your drive, we provide a thoughtfully designed benefits package created to help you thrive both at work and beyond.
Competitive remuneration and a performance-based bonus system;
Shorter workday on Fridays – we finish at 3:00 PM;
5 extra days off at 5 years of service, plus 1 more each year after – up to 10;
2 extra paid days off for volunteering to support the causes you care about;
Premium additional health insurance coverage and annual medical check-ups;
Modern and cozy offices across Bulgaria, plus hybrid work options;
Free parking and a metro shuttle;
Chef-prepared breakfast and lunch provided daily at our HQ restaurant – all on us;
Fully equipped in-office gym with expert fitness guidance;
On-site sports at our HQ: yoga, spinning, Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu, dancing, table tennis, and more;
Multisport or Coolfit cards fully covered by the company;
Free massages;
Memorable team events and internal gatherings;
Knowledge-sharing culture through meetups, events, and conferences;
Free employee access to the SiteGround products;
Anniversary and company gifts along the way.
Come and
make a difference at SiteGround
with people who inspire you to grow!
Please note:
only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for further steps.
We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.

Xebia
is a global AI-first, digital transformation, and engineering partner. With over 25 years of experience and a team of 5,000 professionals across 16 countries, we help organizations design and build scalable products, platforms, and data-driven solutions.
We specialize in Artificial Intelligence, Data and Cloud, Intelligent Automation, and Digital Products, combining deep technical expertise with a strong focus on engineering excellence and a people-first culture.
In the CEE region, we’re a team of nearly 1,000 experts delivering modern applications, data platforms, and AI solutions for clients such as McLaren, Aviva, Deloitte, Spotify, Disney, ING, UPS, Tesco, Truecaller, AllSaints, Volotea, Schmitz Cargobull, Allegro, InPost, and many, many more. We work with leading technologies including AWS, Azure, GCP, Databricks, and Snowflake, and combine strong engineering culture with a consulting mindset and a continuous focus on growth and knowledge sharing.
Join a small, tight-knit product team building an AI-powered, autonomous accounting platform for the smallest businesses and the accountants who serve them.
You’ll own features end-to-end — from an idea in a conversation, through the API and data model, to what the customer actually sees and trusts. A core part of the work is building AI agents and the tools and workflows around them, in a product that’s live in production, not a pilot. This is a Senior-level role. What you’ll do – Build and improve the product experiences small business owners and accountants use every day – Develop backend services and integrations with the systems accounting runs on – Design and ship reliable AI-powered workflows (LLM APIs, tool calling, streaming, agent flows) where „usually right“ is not good enough – Improve reliability and performance, and keep the codebase a good place to work – Work closely with product, engineering, and domain experts to take ideas all the way to customers
You will be:
Minimum 6 years of commercial experience in fullstack software development;
Backend: Node.js + Express, strong command of TypeScript;
Frontend: React and Next.js (SSR/SSG, App Router);
Designing and building REST APIs (GraphQL a plus);
PostgreSQL – data modeling and query optimization;
Testing: unit and integration tests (e.g. Jest/Vitest);
CI/CD and containerization (Docker);
Experience with the cloud (AWS / GCP / Azure);
Hands-on AI/LLM production experience: LLM APIs, tool calling, streaming, prompting, or agent workflows;
AI-native: daily work with AI development tools (e.g. Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Claude Code);
Ability to verify, debug, and refactor AI-generated code;
Your profile:
Self-reliance and ownership – driving a task from analysis through to deployment;
Ability to make architectural decisions and justify them;
Clear technical communication with the team and stakeholders;
Experience in a startup or small, fast-moving team;
Practical experience using AI-powered assistants (e.g. Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor) to improve productivity, quality, or decision-making in software delivery;
Work from the European Union region and a work permit are required.
Nice to have:
Experience with NoSQL databases (e.g. MongoDB, Redis);
Building AI features: RAG, embeddings, prompt engineering, agents;
End-to-end testing (Playwright / Cypress);
Microservices architecture and monorepo experience (Nx / Turborepo);
Cloud certifications (AWS/GCP/Azure);
ORM familiarity (e.g. Prisma, TypeORM);
Experience applying GenAI in a more structured way within the SDLC, including defined workflows, prompt patterns, or tool integrations embedded into daily work;
Interest in and familiarity with emerging AI-driven practices (e.g. agent-based workflows, automation patterns, AI-augmented development), with a willingness to explore and experiment beyond standard approaches;
